{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>עד אנה יהוה</b> The word אנה is found for time and for place, and likewise the word הלום, as in 'אנה אנחנו עולים' (Numbers 13:1), where the meaning is: to which place are we going up." "<b>אזעק אליך</b> Like the cry of a man against whom violence has been done."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra's cross-reference is to the word אנה as it appears in Numbers; the sense is that אנה can mean 'where' (place) or 'when'/'how long' (time)."}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:49.274440606Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}